---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research Workflow"
  description="The A–E DFT research workflow, from structures to target calculations and research completion."
  current="operations"
>
  <h1>Research Workflow</h1>
  <p class="page-intro">
    The workflow is organized around tasks that researchers plan and discuss as meaningful units of work. A–C establish the structure, setup, and reference state; D branches into the calculations required by the scientific question; E turns the results into a supported and reproducible conclusion.
  </p>

  <section class="part-section" id="part-a" aria-labelledby="part-a-heading">
    <header>
      <h2 id="part-a-heading">A · Structures</h2>
      <p>Obtain a trustworthy structure and build the model required by the study.</p>
    </header>
    <ul class="directory-list">
      <li><strong>Obtain a Material Structure</strong><br />Database, publication, experiment, previous calculation, or generated structure; source, parsing, identity, and crystallographic inspection belong within this task.</li>
      <li><strong>Build or Modify a Computational Model</strong><br />Supercells, slabs, defects, adsorbates, interfaces, heterostructures, constraints, magnetic candidates, and disorder models.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="part-section" id="part-b" aria-labelledby="part-b-heading">
    <header>
      <h2 id="part-b-heading">B · Calculation Preparation</h2>
      <p>Choose a physically appropriate setup and establish numerical reliability.</p>
    </header>
    <ul class="directory-list">
      <li><strong>Choose the DFT Method and Computational Setup</strong><br />Physical approximation, core treatment, basis or representation, spin, relativity, interactions, boundaries, occupations, and sampling.</li>
      <li><strong>Test Numerical Convergence</strong><br />Converge the settings that control the intended observable and comparison.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="part-section" id="part-c" aria-labelledby="part-c-heading">
    <header>
      <h2 id="part-c-heading">C · Reference-State Calculations</h2>
      <p>Establish the structure and electronic state used by later calculations.</p>
    </header>
    <ul class="directory-list">
      <li><strong>Optimize the Structure</strong><br />Atomic, lattice, constrained, interface, or other relevant structural degrees of freedom.</li>
      <li><strong>Calculate the Reference Ground State</strong><br />Produce the consistent electronic reference needed by the target calculation.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="part-section" id="part-d" aria-labelledby="part-d-heading">
    <header>
      <h2 id="part-d-heading">D · Target Calculations</h2>
      <p>Each concrete calculation may be documented independently. The group headings are navigation categories, not extra operations.</p>
    </header>

    <h3>D1 · Energetics and Stability</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Relative Energies and Formation Energies</li>
      <li>Equation of State and Structural Phase Stability</li>
      <li>Compositional Phase Stability and Convex Hulls</li>
      <li>Defect Formation Energies and Charge States</li>
      <li>Surface Energy and Work Function</li>
      <li>Adsorption Energies</li>
      <li>Interface and Heterostructure Energetics</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>D2 · Electronic and Magnetic Properties</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Band Structure</li>
      <li>Density of States and Projected Density of States</li>
      <li>Fermi Surface and Full-Brillouin-Zone Analysis</li>
      <li>Charge Density and Charge Redistribution</li>
      <li>Electrostatic Potential and Band Alignment</li>
      <li>Chemical Bonding Analysis</li>
      <li>Magnetic Configuration and Ground-State Comparison</li>
      <li>Magnetic Anisotropy and Exchange Interactions</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>D3 · Mechanical, Electric, and Lattice Response</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Elastic Constants and Mechanical Properties</li>
      <li>Dielectric Response and Born Effective Charges</li>
      <li>Polarization and Ferroelectricity</li>
      <li>Piezoelectric Response</li>
      <li>Harmonic Phonons</li>
      <li>Anharmonic Phonons</li>
      <li>Lattice Thermal Transport</li>
      <li>Electron–Phonon Coupling</li>
      <li>Conventional Superconductivity</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>D4 · Kinetics and Finite Temperature</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Reaction Paths and Transition States</li>
      <li>Diffusion Barriers</li>
      <li>Ab Initio Molecular Dynamics</li>
      <li>Finite-Temperature Structural Sampling</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>D5 · Optical, Excited-State, Topological, and Transport Calculations</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Independent-Particle Optical Properties</li>
      <li>Time-Dependent Response and Spectroscopy</li>
      <li>Quasiparticle Corrections</li>
      <li>Excitons and the Bethe–Salpeter Equation</li>
      <li>Wannier Function Construction</li>
      <li>Berry Phase and Berry Curvature</li>
      <li>Topological Invariants and Boundary States</li>
      <li>Electronic Transport</li>
      <li>Quantum Transport</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="part-section" id="part-e" aria-labelledby="part-e-heading">
    <header>
      <h2 id="part-e-heading">E · Research Completion</h2>
      <p>Turn calculations into an interpretable, supported, and reusable study.</p>
    </header>
    <ul class="directory-list">
      <li><strong>Analyze and Compare Results</strong><br />Normalize, align, aggregate, compare, and interpret the calculated quantities.</li>
      <li><strong>Validate Results and Scientific Conclusions</strong><br />Separate numerical completion, physical consistency, method robustness, and support for the stated conclusion.</li>
      <li><strong>Document and Preserve the Study</strong><br />Record provenance, evidence, software environment, derived data, and reconstruction instructions.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="framework-note">
    Older direct links remain temporarily available while their useful content is migrated. They are not part of the current reading structure.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
